        {
          "post_id": "497597",
          "text": "<p>CONSIDER A COMPUTER C1 CONFIGURED AS FOLLOWS:</p><ul><li><strong>IP ADDRESS:</strong>&nbsp;$\\texttt{192.168.10.100}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>SUBNET MASK:</strong> $\\texttt{255.255.255.192}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>DEFAULT GATEWAY:</strong> $\\texttt{192.168.10.65}$<br>&nbsp;</li></ul><p>C1 WANTS TO SEND A PACKET TO A SECOND COMPUTER, C2, WHICH HAS THE IP ADDRESS $\\texttt{192.168.10.200}$.</p><p>WHICH IP ADDRESS WILL C1 SEND AN ARP REQUEST FOR?<br>&nbsp;</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$\\texttt{192.168.10.200}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\texttt{192.168.10.65}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\texttt{192.168.10.64}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\texttt{192.168.10.127}$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "subject": "Computer Networks",
          "day": "Day 132"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "497588",
          "text": "<p>A SENDER USES THE <strong>SELECTIVE REPEAT</strong> SLIDING WINDOW PROTOCOL AND USES $\\mathbf{7}$&nbsp;<strong>BITS</strong> FOR THE SEQUENCE NUMBER.</p><ul><li>DATA PACKETS ARE $\\mathbf{1}$ <strong>KB</strong> ($1000$ BYTES) IN SIZE.<br>&nbsp;</li><li>THE ONE-WAY PROPAGATION DELAY IS $\\mathbf{2 5}$&nbsp;<strong>msec.</strong><br>&nbsp;</li><li>ASSUME $W_S=W_R$ AND THE TOTAL SEQUENCE SPACE IS FULLY UTILIZED.<br>&nbsp;</li></ul><p>WHAT IS THE MINIMUM LINK BANDWIDTH (IN Mbps) REQUIRED TO ACHIEVE A LINK UTILIZATION OF EXACTLY $\\mathbf{8 0 \\%}$ ?<br>&nbsp;</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$10.1$ Mbps<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$12.6$ Mbps<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$14.2$ Mbps<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$20.5$ Mbps</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "subject": "Computer Networks",
          "day": "Day 132"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "497594",
          "text": "<p>CONSIDER THE ENTRIES SHOWN BELOW IN THE FORWARDING TABLE OF AN IP ROUTER. THE NOTATION '/N' IN A PREFIX INDICATES A SUBNET MASK WITH THE MOST SIGNIFICANT N BITS SET TO $1$.<br><br>\\begin{array}{}<br>\\text { PREFIX } & \\text { NEXT HOP ROUTER } \\\\<br>\\texttt{10.10.0.0 / 16} &nbsp; & \\text{R1} \\\\<br>\\texttt{10.10.128.0 / 18} & \\text{R2} \\\\<br>\\texttt{10.10.192.0 / 20} & \\text{R3} \\\\<br>\\texttt{0.0.0.0 / 0} &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;& \\text{R4} \\\\<br>\\end{array}</p><p><br>ON WHICH INTERFACE WILL THE ROUTER FORWARD PACKETS ADDRESSED TO DESTINATIONS $\\texttt{10.10.140.50}$ AND $\\texttt{172.16.1.1}$ RESPECTIVELY?<br>&nbsp;</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$\\text{R1}$ AND $\\text{R4}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\text{R2}$ AND $\\text{R3}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\text{R2}$ AND $\\text{R4}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\text{R1}$ AND $\\text{R3}$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "subject": "Computer Networks",
          "day": "Day 132"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "497584",
          "text": "<p>A SENDER USES THE <strong>GO-BACK-N</strong> SLIDING WINDOW PROTOCOL.<br>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>DATA PACKETS ARE $\\mathbf{2000}$ BYTES ($1$ BYTE = $8$ BITS).<br>&nbsp;</li><li>THE LINK BANDWIDTH IS $\\mathbf{4}$ <strong>Mbps</strong> ( $4 \\times 10^6$ BITS/SECOND).<br>&nbsp;</li><li>THE ONE-WAY PROPAGATION DELAY IS $\\mathbf{100}$ <strong>msec.</strong><br>&nbsp;</li><li>THE SEQUENCE NUMBER FIELD IS $\\mathbf{5}$&nbsp;<strong>BITS</strong> WIDE.<br>&nbsp;</li></ul><p>ASSUMING NO ERRORS AND NEGLIGIBLE ACKNOWLEDGEMENT TIME, WHAT IS THE MAXIMUM POSSIBLE LINK UTILIZATION?<br>&nbsp;</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$100\\%$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$75.5\\%$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$60.8 \\%$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$50.0 \\%$</li></ol>",
