        {
          "post_id": "497583",
          "text": "<p>CONSIDER A NETWORK WITH $5$ ROUTERS (A TO E). THE LINKS AND THEIR WEIGHTS ARE GIVEN BY THE FOLLOWING GRAPH CODE. THE DISTANCE VECTOR ALGORITHM IS USED TO FIND ALL SHORTEST PATHS.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p><br>SUPPOSE ALL LINKS <em>NOT</em> EXPLICITLY SHOWN IN THE DIAGRAM (SUCH AS A-D, A-E, AND B-E) ARE ADDED TO THE NETWORK. ALL OF THESE NEW LINKS ARE ASSIGNED A WEIGHT OF $2$. THE ALGORITHM IS RUN AGAIN UNTIL ALL ROUTING TABLES STABILIZE.</p><p>WHAT WILL BE THE NEW SHORTEST PATH COST FROM ROUTER <strong>A</strong> TO ROUTER <strong>E</strong>?<br>&nbsp;</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$1$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$2$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$3$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$4$</li></ol>",
